<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>The camera is used for the "Find the aurora" viewfinder, which shows you where to look in the sky. Images are never saved or sent.</string>
	<key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Norður reads from Health the activities you choose to import (for example from Garmin Connect or Apple Watch): GPS route, distance, duration, altitude and heart rate. It writes nothing to Health.</string>
	<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>With “Always” access Norður checks weather warnings, gusts and closed roads near you even when the app is closed, and keeps recording your drive with the screen locked.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Norður uses your location for weather, warnings, roads and aurora where you are, and to record your drives.</string>
	<key>NSMotionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Motion data tells where the phone is pointing, to guide you towards the aurora.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
